{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.not_selfSquare_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.not_selfSquare_linear","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L130-L143","doc":"**The conjecture has content: a concrete refuting witness.**\n\nThe *linear* alternative — a shell space whose `q`-dimension is the angular\n`[n]_q` itself rather than its self-square — fails the class at `q = 2`,\n`n = 2`: `2² - (1/2)² = 15/4` but `(15/4)² = 225/16`.\n\nSo `ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare` is not satisfied by every `shellDim`, and is not\nan empty marker in the sense of the `proof-no-empty-prop-carrier` /\n`proof-claims-unencoded` criteria. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.subshell_decomposition_of_self_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.subshell_decomposition_of_self_square","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L110-L128","doc":"**Derived from the conjecture: the sub-shell decomposition.**\n\nConditional on `ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare`, the shell space at level `n`\ndecomposes into sub-shells of `q`-dimension `[2ℓ+1]_q` for\n`ℓ = 0, …, n-1` — the `ℓ`-tower with its cutoff, and with the *`q`-deformed*\nmultiplicities, not merely the `q = 1` integers `2ℓ+1`.\n\nThis is the §3b-cond non-degenerate shape: the class carries the *hypothesis*\n(the shell space is a self-square), and the conclusion — an observable\nsub-shell structure — is **derived** from it through `qCG_self_square`, not\nprojected back out of a field.  It is also the sharp empirical content of the\nconjecture: an experiment that resolved sub-shell multiplicities departing\nfrom `[2ℓ+1]_q` would refute the identification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare.isSelfSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare.isSelfSquare","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The shell state space at level `n` is the self-square of the angular\nobject: `dim_q 𝒪_n = [n]_q²`, unnormalised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare.unit","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L105-L105","doc":"`q` and `qi` are mutually inverse (the `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` unit relation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellSpaceIsSelfSquare","kind":"class","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L89-L108","doc":"**The conjecture** (`conj:shell-space-is-self-square`), axiomatised as a\ncontent-bearing class per AGENTS.md §3b.\n\n`shellDim n` is the unnormalised `q`-dimension of the *physical* orbital\nstate space at principal level `n` — whatever the substrate hands us.  The\nconjectural content is `isSelfSquare`: that this space is the self-fusion\n`V_n ⊗ V_n` of the single angular object of unnormalised `q`-dimension\n`q^n - qi^n`, so its `q`-dimension is that quantity **squared**.\n\nThis is a **primary** conjecture in the §3b-tax sense: its signature binds no\nother conjecture class.  It is falsifiable — `not_selfSquare_linear` below\nexhibits a concrete `shellDim` that refutes it — and it is *not* satisfied by\nan arbitrary `shellDim`, so the class is not a vacuous marker. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:shell-space-is-self-square","label":"conj:shell-space-is-self-square","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.qCG_self_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.qCG_self_square","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L64-L87","doc":"**`q`-Clebsch–Gordan self-square, division-free, all `n`.**\n\nThe unnormalised form of `[n]_q² = ∑_{ℓ=0}^{n-1} [2ℓ+1]_q`: the self-fusion\n`V ⊗ V` of the `n`-dimensional `SU(2)_q` irrep decomposes into the sub-shell\nirreps of `q`-dimensions `[1]_q, [3]_q, …, [2n-1]_q`.\n\nThis is the **exact** leg of `conj:shell-space-is-self-square`.  It is new\nrelative to `QOU.Molecular.orbital_n_squared`, which proves only the `q = 1`\ninteger specialisation `∑_{ℓ<n} (2ℓ+1) = n²`; the `q`-deformed identity was\npreviously only checked symbolically for `n = 1…8` in\n`computations/shell_capacity_chebyshev_bridge.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.pow_mul_pow_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.pow_mul_pow_unit","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-space-is-self-square.lean#L58-L62","doc":"`q^m · qi^m = 1` for every `m`, from the unit relation `q · qi = 1`.\nLets the `q`-Clebsch–Gordan induction stay inside `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}